        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "An extruded Texas slab with grooved county lines and layered stone walls, casting an attached shadow on a blue sweep. A lighter tinted sheet sits close over it, and a box satellite with one solar wing is upper right with a pale beam below it.",
        "visual_consequence": "Every county, coast and Rio Grande included, sits under the accent sheet, so the image says one instrument in orbit read the whole state without the headline. At the lower opacity the county grooves read crisper through the sheet, and the sheet still shows as a distinct tinted layer with a glass rim.",
        "weakness": "Minor. The sheet reads peach or salmon more than dusk gold. A clear glass rim runs past the panhandle and the far west edge. The beam is a faint wedge that lands near the slab's east edge. The satellite is a plain box with one flat panel.",
        "repair": "none required",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
